# Trivy ignore list for the contextmatrix-agent worker-image scan.
#
# The worker-image-scan job fails on CRITICAL/HIGH vulnerabilities that have an
# upstream fix (ignore-unfixed: true). Every entry must carry a justification;
# review on each worker-image / Go-dependency bump and delete entries whose fix
# has shipped. Dependabot (.github/dependabot.yml) tracks the underlying bumps.

# --- The agent binary embeds the Docker SDK (github.com/docker/docker
# v28.5.2+incompatible); CVE-2026-34040 is a Moby *daemon* authorization-bypass,
# fixed in v29.3.1. The agent uses only the Docker *client*, against a trusted
# local daemon, so the daemon-side authz path is not reachable - govulncheck
# (which is call-graph aware) reports no finding for it. The v28 -> v29 fix is a
# major SDK bump; Dependabot will raise it as a reviewable PR. Accepted until
# then.
CVE-2026-34040

# --- The apt-installed GitHub CLI (/usr/bin/gh, latest release v2.97.0) is a
# prebuilt upstream binary compiled with Go 1.26.5; these are stdlib and
# vendored x/net findings in that embedded toolchain, fixed in Go 1.26.6.
# Everything this repo compiles is already on 1.26.7 (builder image, in-image
# toolchain, agent binary - all scan clean); only GitHub's release pipeline can
# rebuild gh. Inside the worker container repo-controlled code already executes
# arbitrary bash, so these DoS/parsing issues add no marginal attack surface.
# Clears when apt pulls a gh release built on Go >= 1.26.6. (The previous entry
# here, CVE-2026-39822 against a Go 1.26.4 gh, cleared when v2.97.0 shipped.)
CVE-2026-33818
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-46600
CVE-2026-56853
CVE-2026-56858
CVE-2026-56859
CVE-2026-56860
CVE-2026-56862

# --- The bundled npm CLI ships brace-expansion 5.0.7
# (/usr/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/brace-expansion); the fixes land in
# 5.0.8 and 5.0.9. DoS via glob brace expansion inside the npm CLI - the
# single-tenant worker only expands globs npm generates itself. npm's own
# transitive dependency: 11.19.0 (the newest npm that supports Node 25) still
# bundles 5.0.7 - clears when an npm upgrade pulls in >= 5.0.9.
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152

# --- The bundled npm CLI ships ip-address 10.2.0
# (/usr/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/ip-address); the fix is 10.3.1.
# SSRF-shaped parse inconsistency on npm's socks-proxy path, which the worker
# does not configure. npm's own transitive dependency: 11.19.0 still bundles
# 10.2.0 - clears when an npm upgrade pulls in >= 10.3.1.
CVE-2026-69192

# --- The bundled npm CLI ships tar 7.5.19
# (/usr/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/tar); the fix is 7.5.21. DoS via a
# crafted long-path tar archive - inside the npm CLI the only archives tar
# reads are registry tarballs npm fetches itself on the single-tenant worker.
# npm's own transitive dependency: 11.19.0 (the newest npm that supports
# Node 25) and 12.0.2 both still bundle 7.5.19 - clears when an npm release
# pulls in >= 7.5.21.
CVE-2026-73566

# --- The uv-managed CPython (/opt/python) bundles pip, whose _vendor tree pins
# msgpack==1.1.2 and setuptools==70.3.0 (pip/_vendor/vendor.txt - Trivy reads
# the pins as installed packages). GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 (msgpack Unpacker-reuse
# out-of-bounds read, fixed in 1.2.1) touches only pip's deserialization of its
# own local HTTP cache. CVE-2025-47273 (setuptools PackageIndex path traversal,
# fixed in 78.1.1) lives in package_index.py, which pip's vendored copy does not
# ship - only the pkg_resources subset of setuptools is vendored. The pins
# cannot be raised independently of pip, and the latest pip (26.2) still carries
# both - clears when a pip release re-vendors msgpack >= 1.2.1 and setuptools
# >= 78.1.1.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273

# --- golang.org/x/text v0.36.0 inside the golangci-lint binary
# (/usr/local/bin/golangci-lint); the fix is v0.39.0. DoS on invalid UTF-8
# input to a lint binary running repo-controlled code that can already execute
# arbitrary bash. The latest golangci-lint release (v2.12.2) pins v0.36.0 and
# `go install pkg@version` cannot raise a module's own dependency pins -
# clears when a golangci-lint release requires x/text >= v0.39.0.
CVE-2026-56852

# --- golang.org/x/mod v0.35.0 inside the golangci-lint binary
# (/usr/local/bin/golangci-lint); the fix is v0.40.0. Both CVEs are
# sumdb-related module-content forgery (CVE-2026-56864: malicious GOSUMDB
# serves arbitrary module content; CVE-2026-56865: malicious GOPROXY forges
# up to two sumdb entries). The linter runs repo-controlled code that can
# already execute arbitrary bash, so these add no marginal attack surface.
# The latest golangci-lint release (v2.12.2) pins v0.35.0 and `go install
# pkg@version` cannot raise a module's own dependency pins - clears when a
# golangci-lint release requires x/mod >= v0.40.0.
CVE-2026-56864
CVE-2026-56865
